{"title":"Abundance lacking!","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/923970008/0/marginalrevolution~Abundance-lacking.html","date":1756390939000,"content":"<blockquote>\r\n<p>Amtrak is launching a new high-speed Acela train, but there is one wrinkle: It isn’t actually faster, yet.</p>\r\n<p>Five next-generation Acela trains begin service Thursday as part of a $2.45 billion project to improve service along the key Washington-to-Boston corridor. But two of them running from Washington to Boston will actually travel more slowly than their predecessors do on the same route Thursday, according to a Wall Street Journal analysis of Amtrak’s schedule. These new trains are scheduled to take at least seven hours and five minutes to complete the trip, compared with the average time of six hours and 56 minutes on the older Acela trains.</p>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n<p>Here is <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.wsj.com/us-news/amtraks-new-acela-trains-are-here-theyre-moving-slower-than-the-old-ones-f0794127?mod=hp_lead_pos11\" target=\"_blank\">more from the WSJ</a>.  Via <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://x.com/anecdotal\" target=\"_blank\">Anecdotal</a>.</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/08/abundance-lacking.html\">Abundance lacking!</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/923970008/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/923970008/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/923970008/marginalrevolution,\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/pinterest20.png\" /></a> <a